- Spec = docs/knowledge/throttling.md (read it fully; cite its tags). Operator: "a hex that doesn't mean anything to me"; wants XTU-style point-in-time
  Power / Current / Thermal indicators that flip as conditions change, plus logging.
- Orchestrator decision (record as one line in telemetry-sources.md): ADD 0x6B1 (ring perf limit reasons, package, read-only) to TELEMETRY_MSRS — plain rdmsr,
  telemetry set only; NOT PLAIN_MSR_READABLE. Fix the msrio.py:8-10 docstring conflict (sets are separate).
- NO MSR WRITES anywhere: never clear log bits (0x64F/0x6B0/0x6B1/0x19C/0x1B1). "Reset" = app counters only.
- Sampler: 0x64F on CPU 0 at ~10 Hz inside the existing sampler thread (cheap: CPU 0 only); publish per tick per group: active (status OR over the window),
  duty (fraction of samples), bits list. 0x1B1 once per tick. 0x19C per CPU only on demand (a `detail` flag on telemetry.start args if trivial; else skip, say so).
  Kernel thermal_throttle/*_count diff per tick as `kernel_thermal` (sysfs, root-free).
- Groups (labels exactly): "Power limit" (bits 10 PL1 / 11 PL2), "Current / EDP" (8 electrical/other, 7 VR TDC), "Thermal" (1 thermal, 0 PROCHOT, 5 RATL),
  "VR thermal" (6), "Max turbo cap" (12, grey/info, never amber), attenuation/residency (13/4) popover only; unknown bits shown by number only.
- UI: the Dashboard tile and the monitor strip drop the hex: chips Power · Current/EDP · Thermal · VR thermal (green "No" / amber-red "Yes" with duty %),
  grey Max-turbo chip, click -> popover (every active status bit, SDM name, source word, "log since boot" bits flagged "may have been cleared by XTU on Windows").
  Keep the raw words only in the popover. Retire limit_reasons_raw from the UI.
- Event log: throttle.jsonl beside the audit log (dev $XDG_STATE_HOME/arltuner/, installed /var/lib/arltuner/, D-030/D-041), written by the helper sampler,
  0600, size-capped rotation, debounce per §E (open on first window, close after 2 clean windows; max-turbo not logged). Fields per §E incl. tuning_id (accepted
  name / last apply id). Read op `throttle.tail {n}` (bounded) — add it to the Rust allowlist (desktop/app/src-tauri/src/helper/ops.rs; you may edit it ONLY for
  that) and a "Throttle events" list (Dashboard card or Audit sub-section; your choice, say which).
- Other workers are editing src/arltuner/guard/*, controls/*, helper/ops_tune.py (G-226) and desktop/app/ui/views/tune/* (G-227): do not touch those.
- Simulator/fake sysfs only; the simulator should be able to produce throttle bits (add a knob) for tests and the mock. Do NOT run build-appimage.sh.
